# Files Semgrep should skip entirely.
#
# scripts/fetch-catalogs.ts is a Node build-time helper invoked only via
# `npm run fetch-catalogs` (and as the `prebuild` step). It is never
# bundled into the SPA or executed in users' browsers. The execSync call
# inside `run()` is composed from a hardcoded framework list literal
# (`["soc2", "iso27001"]`) — there is no user input path into the
# child_process call, so the `detect-child-process` rule is a false
# positive. Inline `// nosemgrep` directives are not honored by
# `semgrep ci` v1.163.0 in this CI configuration, so the suppression
# lives here instead.
scripts/fetch-catalogs.ts
